After having played mostly [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marathon_(video_game) Marathon on Mac], Xerial got a PC and discovered Quake in 1997, while reading the PC gamer issue that covered [[Quake SM '97]]. He played mostly on local LAN parties in Eskilstuna together with {{Player|Ztorm|flag=se}} and at that time recently transitioned RQ player {{Player|Wretch|flag=se}}, who was associated with [[Clan Tjack]]. As an HPW he made brief appearances in some clans sporadically and organized local LAN parties in Eskilstuna. 

Gaining access to an ISDN connection 98/99, Xerial joined [[Da Imperial Executors]] and was taken under the wings of more senior player {{Player|Scarym|flag=se}}, who trained him to play proper 2on2 on DM6, skills Xerial began to leverage also on other maps shortly thereafter. In 2000, Xerial participated in a small 16 man LAN named dunnolan arranged by {{Player|Malo|flag=se}} in Uppsala, where he teamed up with {{Player|Nikita|flag=se}}, {{Player|Angua|flag=se}} and {{Player|Javve|flag=se}} under the [[Spartacus]] flag. Although no official tournament was held, they had success against [[Swedish Chefs]], [[Clan Dunno]] and began playing together online.
